course: dictionary
lesson: 8629
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Scrum is one of them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer wants. «In rugby the ball may only be passed sideways or backwards; a forward pass gives the other team a scrum.» The word rugby is the clue, so here a scrum is a way of restarting play in a rugby match.
explain: Scrum also has an everyday meaning. A crowd of people pushing to get somewhere can be called a scrum, like the crush at the school gate. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Computer teams use the word too. Programmers plan their work in short bursts called sprints, and the way they plan it is called scrum. The subject of the text, whether sport, crowds or computers, tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: In rugby, a scrum is a way of restarting play. Players from each team pack together with arms linked, push against each other and try to win the ball with their feet.
fact: Scrum can also be an informal word for a crowd pushing to get somewhere or something.
fact: In computing and work, scrum is a way teams plan their work in short bursts called sprints.
fact: Scrum can be a verb too: players scrum down, which means they form a scrum.
exercise: In rugby, what does scrum mean? | *A way of restarting play, with players packed together | A long run to the try line | A pile of rubbish left on the pitch | A type of cap worn for protection
exercise: «In rugby the ball may only be passed sideways or backwards; a forward pass gives the other team a scrum.» Find the word that tells you the sport. | *rugby | forward | passed | ball
exercise: Programmers plan their work in short bursts. What are these bursts called in scrum? | Laps | Tries | *Sprints | Scrums
test: Rugby players scrum down before the ball goes in. What does scrum down mean? | Sit down for a rest | Run away fast | Catch the ball in the air | *Pack together to form a scrum
test: Everyday talk uses scrum for a crush at the school gate. What does scrum mean there? | A type of bell | Calm and quiet | A sports team's cap | *A crowd of people pushing to get somewhere
exam: Ella reads «a media scrum» in the news and asks what it means. Which answer uses the clues best? | A cap for the head | A calm talk with one reporter | A rugby pass | *A crowd of reporters pushing to get the story
